\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Hark, my soul! It is the Lord;
\par \pard\li225\sl180\slmult0 Tis thy Saviour, hear His word;
\par Jesus speaks, and speaks to thee:
\par 'Say, poor sinner, loves thou Me?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2. I delivered thee when bound,
\par \pard\li225\sl180\slmult0 and when bleeding, healed thy wound;
\par sought thee wandering, set thee right;
\par turned thy darkness into light.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3. Can a woman's tender care
\par \pard\li225\sl180\slmult0  cease towards the child she bare?
\par  Yes, she may forgetful be,
\par  Yet will I remember thee.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.    Mine is an unchanging love,
\par \pard\li225\sl180\slmult0 higher than the heights above,
\par  deeper than the depths beneath,
\par   free and faithful, strong as death.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   5.   Thou shall see My glory soon,
\par \pard\li225\sl180\slmult0   When the work of grace is done;
\par    Partner of My throne shall be;
\par     Say, poor sinner, loves thou Me?'
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.   Lord, it is my chief complaint
\par \pard\li225\sl180\slmult0    That my love is weak and faint;
\par  Yet I love Thee, and adore;
\par \pard       O for grace to love Thee more!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

